# Peanut Noodles

Source: Former coworkers Dani and Michael

{ rating="2" image="peanut_noodles.jpg" }
:::
:::

## Ingredients

- [ ] Garnish Options

      - [ ] [Sesame seeds]{ ing="sesame-seeds" } (or Peanuts)
      - [ ] [Green onions]{ ing="green-onions" }, sliced
      - [ ] [Cilantro]{ ing="cilantro" }
      - [ ] [shrimp]{ ing="shrimp" }, _marinated in lime, salt, and garlic powder then sautéed_
- [ ] Peanut Noodles

      - [ ] [linguine]{ ing="linguine" }, egg noodles, or rice
      - [ ] [chopped baby carrots]{ ing="chopped-baby-carrots" }
      - [ ] [chopped shallots]{ ing="chopped-shallots" } (a.k.a. white base of green onion)
      - [ ] _other vegetables: peppers, broccoli, zucchini, snow peas_
- [ ] Sauce

      - [ ] 6 Tbsp [pb]{ ing="pb" }
      - [ ] 1.5 Tbsp [hot chili oil]{ ing="hot-chili-oil" }
      - [ ] 2 Tbsp [sesame oil]{ ing="sesame-oil" }
      - [ ] 7 Tbsp [soy sauce]{ ing="soy-sauce" }
      - [ ] 2 tsp [cider vinegar]{ ing="cider-vinegar" } (or white wine/rice vinegar)
      - [ ] 1 inch fresh [ginger]{ ing="ginger" } (or 1.5 tsp cinnamon, nutmeg, or sugar)

## Recipe

1. Mix the [sauce]{ ing="soy-sauce" } until smooth and prep the vegetables separately
1. Boil the pasta, drain, then immediately toss with vegetables and [sauce]{ ing="soy-sauce" }
